---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, isCommodityNode, site } from '../lib/site-variant';

if (!isCommodityNode) return Astro.redirect('/blog/');
const canonicalUrl = absoluteUrl('/about/');
---

<Base
  title="About CommodityNode"
  description="CommodityNode is an evidence-linked commodity impact intelligence product built on an attributed AGPL fork of WorldMonitor."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <article class="static-page prose">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1>Trace every conclusion back to its evidence.</h1>
    <p class="article-dek">
      CommodityNode maps how physical events travel through assets, routes, benchmarks, companies, and industries. The source trail stays beside the conclusion.
    </p>

    <h2>What we are building</h2>
    <p>
      The live product combines a geographic operating picture with a typed relationship graph. The research site explains the methods, assumptions, and limitations behind those views.
    </p>

    <h2>Open-source foundation</h2>
    <p>
      CommodityNode is built from an attributed fork of WorldMonitor and remains licensed under AGPL-3.0-only. The deployed build publishes its exact commit and corresponding source so users can inspect what is running.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not claim</h2>
    <p>
      A relationship on the map is not proof of price causation. We distinguish reviewed facts,
      reported claims, and analyst inference, and we leave uncertain links unpublished until the
      evidence supports them.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href={site.liveUrl}>Open live intelligence</a> or review the <a href={site.sourceUrl}>source repository</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
